{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChRJjmeugqL56qJkMHnWk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UvwDjoFfmPa3KNG47BN4yT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-ZjfoQZ/memory/sort-customers-by-id-before-export.md","content":"---\nname: sort-customers-by-id-before-export\ndescription: listCustomers() order is unstable in production; always sort customers by id before writing them out in a list (exports, files, reports)\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`listCustomers()` returns customers in the order the store holds them, and in production that order is not stable. Anything that writes customers out in a list must sort them by id first.\n\n**Why:** The nightly customer export kept showing changes when no data had changed. The cause was unstable ordering from `listCustomers()`, not real differences in the data.\n\n**How to apply:** When adding or modifying code that serializes, exports, or otherwise emits a list of customers (files, reports, diffs, snapshots), sort by customer id before writing. Don't rely on the store's order. No code change was made at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26); the existing nightly export may still need the fix.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9684,"cache_read_input_tokens":11962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9684,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7ac61938-d5cb-4563-892a-a977193ebfbc","uuid":"11670c4b-d725-4983-b19e-140d7cbcd5de","timestamp":"2026-11-26T09:31:15.566Z","request_id":"req_011ChRJjmWDpmkrYeVLuBxMX","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UvwDjoFfmPa3KNG47BN4yT":{"file_path":"/Users/johnmarkenriquez/.claude-personal/projects/-private-var-folders-wg-kshmq8sn7zl5m1ch85m7yvvh0000gn-T-invoice-service-ZjfoQZ/memory/sort-customers-by-id-before-export.md","content":"---\nname: sort-customers-by-id-before-export\ndescription: listCustomers() order is unstable in production; always sort customers by id before writing them out in a list (exports, files, reports)\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\n`listCustomers()` returns customers in the order the store holds them, and in production that order is not stable. Anything that writes customers out in a list must sort them by id first.\n\n**Why:** The nightly customer export kept showing changes when no data had changed. The cause was unstable ordering from `listCustomers()`, not real differences in the data.\n\n**How to apply:** When adding or modifying code that serializes, exports, or otherwise emits a list of customers (files, reports, diffs, snapshots), sort by customer id before writing. Don't rely on the store's order. No code change was made at the time this was recorded (2026-11-26); the existing nightly export may still need the fix.\n"}}}
